{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"decorous-eclectic-firecrest","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Problem / opportunity\n\nThe source audit measured a 72.3% first-pass completion-verification rate, but non-PASS outcomes conflate implementation defects, unmet acceptance criteria, missing proof, plan/scope gaps, environment failures, and verifier defects. Treating the aggregate as a code-quality or bug-escape measure would be invalid.\n\n## Prior decisions that constrain this idea\n\nolivine-married-kodiakbear made FAIL verdicts durable; chief-sizeable-skua requires exhaustive unmet-criterion findings; cinnamoned-tzarist-kangaroo added a distinct ERROR outcome; crumply-denim-pitbull persists PASS criteria; earthen-flayed-baboon distinguishes insufficient evidence; beryl-orange-oropendola tallies survived step failures; paralyzed-sane-flyingfox derives gate economics; depressant-amethyst-wasp exposes the audit trail. The historical evaluation's independent reviewer counted 351 failure sidecars with 682 structured findings carrying criterion, dimension, severity, detail, citations, and remediation.\n\nThe project already has the evidence channel. This idea must test derivation before proposing another telemetry or schema surface.\n\n## Outcome hypothesis\n\nHistorical first-non-PASS completion records can be classified into a small, stable cause taxonomy that separates implementation quality from evidence, planning, environment, and verifier failures. The taxonomy can guide targeted prevention and make completion first-pass metrics interpretable.\n\n## Candidate taxonomy\n\n- Code or implementation defect.\n- Acceptance criterion genuinely unmet.\n- Missing test, citation, or other evidence.\n- Plan or scope gap.\n- Environment or integration failure.\n- Verifier or tool failure.\n\nThese are hypotheses, not yet a committed schema.\n\n## Guardrails\n\n- Use existing FAIL, PASS, ERROR, insufficient_evidence, and survived-step records as the primary source.\n- Classify the first non-PASS attempt separately from later remediation outcomes.\n- Preserve source citations and uncertainty; do not force ambiguous findings into a confident category.\n- Do not add required author input or a parallel telemetry channel.\n- Add durable reason codes only if offline derivation is unreliable and the categories prove operationally useful.\n- Keep code defects distinct from missing proof and verifier/tool failures.\n\n## Questions before promotion\n\n- What sampling design covers common and rare sidecar shapes without overrepresenting high-attempt tickets?\n- What labeling rubric yields acceptable independent agreement?\n- Can deterministic rules classify high-confidence cases before an LLM or human-coded adjudicator handles the remainder?\n- Which records legitimately need multiple causes, and what should be primary versus contributing?\n- What agreement/stability threshold justifies durable reason codes?\n- Which downstream metrics or planning checks would consume each category?\n- How will schema/version changes remain additive if derivation proves insufficient?\n\n## Evidence\n\nDiscovered from unpleasing-hairy-yellowlegs; source audit bleakish-stational-cob. Prior work: olivine-married-kodiakbear, chief-sizeable-skua, cinnamoned-tzarist-kangaroo, crumply-denim-pitbull, earthen-flayed-baboon, beryl-orange-oropendola, paralyzed-sane-flyingfox, depressant-amethyst-wasp.","id":"d1b1-d32f-0f4c-4e53","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["process","quality","metrics"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Derive a completion non-PASS cause taxonomy from existing sidecars"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786825448257681001,"uuid":"ea021434-51c2-49b7-9919-3075495368da"}